From e33d1e981da380f4969e2b72bd1ce5d5383a050b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Clasen <d.clasen@qvest-digital.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 08:53:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ice: take the UP to TC map from dcbnl ETS in DSCP mode

ice_dcbnl_setets() copies prio_tc into the desired configuration only
in VLAN QoS mode. In L3 DSCP mode the map is written once, 1:1 up to
the port's maximum TC count, when the first DSCP application entry
switches the port to DSCP mode, and an ETS request's prio_tc is
dropped without an error, while its bandwidth and TSA tables are
applied.

Copy prio_tc in both modes. The driver's map decides the number of
TCs the PF VSI is configured with (ice_dcb_get_num_tc()), the netdev
priority to TC map and the num_tc irdma is given. The LLDP MIB sent
to firmware in DSCP mode carries the DSCP to UP table, TC bandwidth,
TSA, the maximum TC count and PFC, not a UP to TC map, so firmware
configuration is the same for every map.

Entering DSCP mode still writes the 1:1 map, so nothing changes until
an ETS request is made. A request firmware refuses leaves the previous
configuration in place: ice_pf_dcb_cfg() restores it when
ice_set_dcb_cfg() fails.
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_dcb_nl.c | 7 ++-----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_dcb_nl.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_dcb_nl.c
index a10c1c8..f39cae8 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_dcb_nl.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_dcb_nl.c
@@ -85,11 +85,8 @@ static int ice_dcbnl_setets(struct net_device *netdev, struct ieee_ets *ets)
 		new_cfg->etscfg.tcbwtable[i] = ets->tc_tx_bw[i];
 		bwcfg += ets->tc_tx_bw[i];
 		new_cfg->etscfg.tsatable[i] = ets->tc_tsa[i];
-		if (new_cfg->pfc_mode == ICE_QOS_MODE_VLAN) {
-			/* in DSCP mode up->tc mapping cannot change */
-			new_cfg->etscfg.prio_table[i] = ets->prio_tc[i];
-			new_cfg->etsrec.prio_table[i] = ets->reco_prio_tc[i];
-		}
+		new_cfg->etscfg.prio_table[i] = ets->prio_tc[i];
+		new_cfg->etsrec.prio_table[i] = ets->reco_prio_tc[i];
 		new_cfg->etsrec.tcbwtable[i] = ets->tc_reco_bw[i];
 		bwrec += ets->tc_reco_bw[i];
 		new_cfg->etsrec.tsatable[i] = ets->tc_reco_tsa[i];
